Subject: [PATCH] docs: README states the Radeon 780M test system and what
 changes between the 780M and the 890M

A "Test system (Radeon 780M numbers)" section lists the previous machine's BIOS settings, memory epochs, driver, Windows build, power plan (with the measured plan A/B) and Windows settings. A "Radeon 780M vs Radeon 890M" section explains that both GPUs get the same kernel settings at every verify width, the one compute-unit-based difference, where each default was tuned, the best draft depth per GPU (4 on the 780M, 6 on the 890M for the 27B) and the memory each line needs. Also: the Escha .escha_aux data is tensors inside the GGUF, not a separate file, and the Q5_K route reverts with `legacy`, not `0`.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native) - release documentation for this fork; no upstream origin exists.
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - documents only; no code path is touched.
